intro="The area of a rectangular plot with a given perimeter, the speed of a train on a journey, or the height of a thrown stone at a given time: such problems lead to equations in which the unknown appears squared. This chapter defines a quadratic equation, solves it by factorisation, by completing the square and by a formula, uses the discriminant to describe the nature of roots, and applies the equations to word problems.",
