("p", "**Example.** For 3x<sup>2</sup> &minus; 4&radic;3 x + 4 = 0: D = 48 &minus; 48 = 0, so equal roots x = 2/&radic;3. **Find k** for which kx(x &minus; 2) + 6 = 0 has equal roots: kx<sup>2</sup> &minus; 2kx + 6 = 0, D = 4k<sup>2</sup> &minus; 24k = 0, **k = 6** (k = 0 rejected). For real roots of x<sup>2</sup> + kx + 9: D = k<sup>2</sup> &minus; 36 &ge; 0, so k &le; &minus;6 or k &ge; 6."),
